  <title>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">Atyrau Refinery LLP</narrative>
  </title>
  <description type="1">
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">Provision of a KZT 60.7 billion (approx. EUR 114 million) debt financing to  Atyrau Oil Refinery LLP (the &quot;Company&quot; or &quot;ANPZ&quot;) split into two tranches under  two loan agreements:    * the first tranche of KZT 34.1 billion, provided under the first loan signed  in June 2021, was used to upgrade process water treatment facilities in  accordance with best available solutions and remediate evaporation ponds  adjacent to the city of Atyrau; and   * the second tranche of KZT 26.6 billion provided under the second loan will  be used to restructure the Company&apos;s balance sheet by refinancing its  short-term debt. Both loans are fully guaranteed by National Company  KazMunayGas JSC (the &quot;sponsor&quot; or &quot;KMG&quot;), the 99.54% shareholder of the Company.  First tranche: Environmental Upgrades  The proceeds from the first tranche are directed toward improving resource  efficiency and reducing emissions by upgrading process water treatment  facilities. This will result in an increased water reuse and resolve  long-standing environmental issues by remediating 860 ha evaporation ponds  adjacent to the city of Atyrau. The proceeds of the tranche align fully with  the Bank&apos;s Green Economy Transition approach and will result in (i) an  improvement of water efficiency, (ii) the minimisation of adverse ecological  impacts by remediating the evaporation ponds, and (iii) a reduction of GHG  emissions and volatile organic compounds.  Second Tranche: Financial Resilience  The objective of the second tranche is to strengthen the Company&apos;s financial  stability by refinancing its short-term debt into a longer-term KZT-denominated  debt, not otherwise accessible on comparable terms and conditions in the  market. This refinancing will enhance ANPZ&apos;s ability to manage liquidity risks  and help sustain its financial resilience.</narrative>
  </description>
